{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":486000,"name":"Loni Riw","username":"Loni_Riw","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/a87d85/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T07:43:21.831Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486000-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486000-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486000-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486000-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot previously worked, but now I cannot access my Bot computer or load my Bots.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInitially, the app showed “Can’t Reach Grok Bot’s Computer” and suggested allowing *.cursorvm.com. It now shows:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCan’t reach your computer. Your Bots are safe, they just can’t be loaded right now. If it doesn’t come back on its own, recover it. Your files and logins are kept, but installed apps and packages are removed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRetry stays on “retrying,” and Recover fails with “unable to reset.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlready tried without success:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFully quit and reopened Grok Bot.\u003cbr\u003e\nSigned out and signed back in.\u003cbr\u003e\nRetried the connection and attempted Recover.\u003cbr\u003e\nNetwork checks:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"http://test123.us9.cursorvm.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003etest123.us9.cursorvm.com\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"http://test123.us10.cursorvm.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003etest123.us10.cursorvm.com\u003c/a\u003e resolve through the configured DNS, ISP DNS, 1.1.1.1, and 8.8.8.8.\u003cbr\u003e\nHTTPS requests to cached computer endpoints under *.cursorvm.com return HTTP 404, confirming DNS/TLS/HTTP connectivity—not that the assigned computer is healthy.\u003cbr\u003e\nWi-Fi HTTP, HTTPS, and SOCKS proxies are disabled.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe remote computer previously accessible through Tailscale was reported offline during troubleshooting.\u003cbr\u003e\nPlease check my assigned cloud computer and any failed or stuck recovery operation. I would like to restore access while preserving my Bots, files, and logins. I cannot access the remote desktop or terminal to troubleshoot it directly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486000-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486000-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen Grok Bot and sign in to my existing account.\u003cbr\u003e\nAttempt to load my existing Bots/computer.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe app displays “Can’t reach your computer.”\u003cbr\u003e\nClick Retry — it remains retrying and does not reconnect.\u003cbr\u003e\nClick Recover — it fails with “unable to reset.”\u003cbr\u003e\nFully quit/reopen and sign out/in — the same issue persists.\u003cbr\u003e\nExpected: The existing computer reconnects, or Recover successfully restores it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eActual: The computer remains inaccessible, and both Retry and Recover fail.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486000-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486000-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/e/0/e00e2db5ead81f2f30e4bc2249a1ddddbe8f5c0f.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/vY5kvAFVtWbGkWXQoUjTjQGTnt5.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-08 at 1.12.14 PM.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/e/0/e00e2db5ead81f2f30e4bc2249a1ddddbe8f5c0f.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-08 at 1.12.14 PM.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"vY5kvAFVtWbGkWXQoUjTjQGTnt5\" width=\"442\" height=\"500\" data-dominant-color=\"1A1A1A\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-09-08 at 1.12.14 PM.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e720×814 26.8 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486000-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486000-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486000-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486000-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProduct: Grok Bot desktop app, not Cursor IDE\u003cbr\u003e\nVersion: 0.44.0\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: macOS 15.6.1\u003cbr\u003e\nIssue observed: September 8, 2026, IST (UTC+05:30); previously working the day before\u003cbr\u003e\nRequest/conversation ID: Not available from the inaccessible Bot screen\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486000-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486000-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T08:10:21.970Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":12,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":60.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171004,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-44-0-macos-can-t-reach-your-computer-retry-and-recover-fail-even-after-re-login","display_username":"Loni Riw","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://test123.us9.cursorvm.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0},{"url":"http://test123.us10.cursorvm.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136742,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-44-0-macos-can-t-reach-your-computer-retry-and-recover-fail-even-after-re-login/171004/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":486044,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T08:08:38.398Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report and the screenshot. I can see that same screen with \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e / Zscaler.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGood news: this isn’t a network issue or DNS, and your Bot computer isn’t “broken”. The cause is different: the 1-week free trial for Grok Bot on your account ended on 6 September at about 1:23 IST, overnight into the 7th. After that, the app can’t connect to the computer anymore, and Retry and Recover can’t fix it because the account doesn’t have active Grok Bot access right now. The app should show this directly instead of “can’t reach your computer”. This is a known issue with how this state is displayed, and I’ve shared this case with the team.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour Bots, files, and logins are saved. They’ll be available again as soon as your account has access:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGo to \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/bot/onboarding\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eSign in\u003c/a\u003e on the same account and pick a plan that includes Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf you already have a SuperGrok subscription on \u003ca href=\"http://grok.com\"\u003egrok.com\u003c/a\u003e, link it at \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/promos/super-grok\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eCursor - The best way to code with AI\u003c/a\u003e using the same email.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThen fully quit Grok Bot from the menu bar icon, reopen it, and sign in with the same account.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf after step 3 you still see “Can’t reach your computer”, reply here and I’ll take another look.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T08:08:38.398Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171004,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-44-0-macos-can-t-reach-your-computer-retry-and-recover-fail-even-after-re-login","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/bot/onboarding","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Sign in","c